#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""seal-gate: two things nothing on this Mac can give itself, because the key is in a phone.

A yes for one command. Something on this Mac holds a risky command (git-guard does, for one). Instead
of a typed "allow", the yes is a signature made by the Seal app on the phone after Face ID, over a
request that names the exact command.

A pass for a stretch of work: the session lock. Agent sessions whose hooks call `seal-gate hook` take
no message and run no tool while no pass is good. A pass is a signature made on the phone after Face
ID, over words that name this Mac and the time the pass ends.

    seal-gate --setup "ecdsa-sha2-nistp256 AAAA... name"    the phone's key (Seal: Sign page, Copy SSH key)

    seal-gate ask   [--in DIR] [--why WORDS] -- git push origin main
    seal-gate check [--in DIR]               -- git push origin main
    seal-gate try                                              one round by hand, timed

    seal-gate pass ask [--for MINUTES]                         30 minutes unless told, 4 hours at most
    seal-gate pass check
    seal-gate pass drop
    seal-gate pass try [--for MINUTES]                         one round by hand, timed
    seal-gate hook
    seal-gate settings

    seal-gate status

    seal-gate pair [KEY LINE]       the phone's key, from the clipboard unless given (refused while the lock is on)
    seal-gate on                    every Claude Code session with the Seal plugin waits for a pass
    seal-gate off                   needs a yes from the phone, asked for and taken through the clipboard
    seal-gate git                   this repository signs its commits through the phone (seal-git-sign)
    seal-gate slash VERB [...]      what the plugin's /seal: commands run: the same, written for the chat

The switch. The Seal plugin's hooks call seal-hook, which lets everything through at once while the
lock is off and calls `seal-gate hook` while it is on. On is a file, lock-on, in this tool's folder.
Off takes a yes signed on the phone over the words "Turn the Seal lock off", so nothing on this Mac
switches it off by itself. While the lock holds, four of the plugin's commands still go through,
each typed alone: /seal:status, /seal:on, /seal:drop and /seal:lockdown.

ask   makes a request for exactly that command in that folder, shows it as one "seal://sign?..." line
      and puts the line on the clipboard. On the phone: Seal, Sign, Paste a signing request, read it,
      Sign with Face ID, Copy the signature. Asking again for the same command gives the same request
      for as long as it is good, so the answer still fits.
check looks for the signature on the clipboard (or on standard input with --stdin). It exits 0 only
      when the real ssh-keygen says the signature was made by the phone's key, for this purpose, over
      the request this tool made for exactly this command and folder, and the request is neither past
      its time nor used before. A yes counts once.

pass ask    makes a request for a pass, shows it as one "seal://sign?..." line and puts the line on
            the clipboard. The phone signs it like any request. Asking again within five minutes gives
            the same request, so the answer still fits.
pass check  exits 0 while a pass is good. It first looks on the clipboard (or on standard input with
            --stdin) for the phone's answer to a waiting request, and keeps a good one. A pass is not
            used up: it is good until its time. It is checked against the phone's key every single
            time, so a pass file written by hand is no pass.
pass drop   locks again now. The same signature cannot bring the pass back.
pass try    asks for a pass and waits three minutes for the phone's answer to arrive on the clipboard:
            the whole trip by hand, with no session involved.
hook        the lock itself, made for Claude Code's hooks UserPromptSubmit and PreToolUse (the event
            comes as JSON on standard input). With a good pass it says nothing and exits 0: it never
            says yes to a tool by itself, so the agent's own rules and questions apply as always. With
            no pass it holds: a tool with exit 2 and words for the agent; a message with Claude Code's
            JSON answer (decision "block"), whose reason the desktop app shows as text, saying how to
            unlock and how to get out. The usual answer is the signature pasted into a message (on the
            Mac, the paste fetches it from the phone); one found on the clipboard counts too. Whatever
            goes wrong inside the lock holds too.
settings    prints the settings that put a Claude Code session under the lock: both hooks, each told
            to hold when the lock cannot even start. For one session and nothing kept:
            claude --settings "$(seal-gate settings)"

What a yes or a pass does not cover: a signature for a file or a git commit never passes here (another
purpose), a yes for a command is no pass and a pass is no yes for a command, and nothing counts unless
the phone signed exactly the words this tool builds: for this command in this folder, or for this Mac
and a time this tool allows.

Said plainly: this tool, its folder (~/.seal-gate) and whatever calls it belong to the same user the
agents run as. Nothing on this Mac can make a yes or a pass, and while no pass is good a session under
the lock can run nothing, so it cannot take the lock off either. But while a pass is good, an agent
set on it can remove the lock itself. It holds against that only if these files belong to an admin
account the agents cannot use.

It talks to no network. The clipboard is the Mac's own (pbcopy, pbpaste); Apple's shared clipboard
carries it to the phone and back when both are signed in to the same account and near each other.
"""
import base64
import contextlib
import fcntl
import hashlib
import io
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import shlex
import shutil
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time


def shorter(name, most):
    """A time from the surroundings can make a wait shorter (for a test), never longer."""
    try:
        return max(1, min(most, int(os.environ.get(name) or most)))
    except ValueError:
        return most


SSH_KEYGEN = os.environ.get("SEAL_SSH_KEYGEN", "/usr/bin/ssh-keygen")
FOLDER = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("SEAL_GATE_DIR", "~/.seal-gate"))
COPY = os.environ.get("SEAL_GATE_COPY", "/usr/bin/pbcopy")
PASTE = os.environ.get("SEAL_GATE_PASTE", "/usr/bin/pbpaste")
NAMESPACE = "seal-agent"
PASS_NAMESPACE = "seal-pass"
WHO = "seal-gate"
# How long a request waits for the phone's answer.
GOOD_FOR = shorter("SEAL_GATE_GOOD_FOR", 300)
LONGEST_COMMAND = 600
# How long a pass is good for: 30 minutes unless told, 4 hours at most.
PASS_USUAL = 30 * 60
PASS_LONGEST = 4 * 60 * 60
PASS_AT_MOST = shorter("SEAL_GATE_PASS_SECONDS", PASS_LONGEST)
BEGIN, END = "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----", "-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----"
# How long a hold gives Apple's shared clipboard to bring a copy over from the phone. It fetches only
# when something reads the clipboard, and 5 seconds was too short in Seth's first real test
# (2026-11-15); the hooks wait 45 seconds in all.
CLIPBOARD_WAIT = 20
# No signature the phone makes comes near this many letters.
LONGEST_SIGNATURE = 8192
PARTS = ("", "pending", "used", "pass", os.path.join("pass", "ended"))


# Lockdown: the lock installed by `seal-lockdown` (run with sudo) into Claude Code's admin-owned
# settings, which no user, project or local setting can switch off. Its files live here, owned by root.
# The tests point it elsewhere for the user-run commands. The hooks never take it from the surroundings:
# seal-hook checks the fixed path, and the lockdown's own hook gets it as an argument.
LOCKDOWN_ROOT = os.environ.get("SEAL_LOCKDOWN_ROOT", "/Library/Application Support/Seal")
MANAGED_SETTINGS = "/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json"
LOCKDOWN = False


def own_home():
    """The home folder the system says this user has: not $HOME, which a project's settings could change."""
    import pwd
    return pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir


def harden(lockdown_root=None, state=None, copy=None, paste=None):
    """For the hooks: take nothing from the surroundings. A project's settings can set environment
    variables for a session, and with them once pointed the lock at an empty folder (security review
    H1). The hook then uses the system's own tools, the user's real home and fixed times. In lockdown
    the phone's key is read from the root-owned folder, and the lock is on whatever any file says."""
    global FOLDER, SSH_KEYGEN, COPY, PASTE, GOOD_FOR, PASS_AT_MOST, SIGNERS, LOCKDOWN, LOCKDOWN_ROOT
    FOLDER = state or os.path.join(own_home(), ".seal-gate")
    SSH_KEYGEN = "/usr/bin/ssh-keygen"
    COPY = copy or "/usr/bin/pbcopy"
    PASTE = paste or "/usr/bin/pbpaste"
    GOOD_FOR = 300
    PASS_AT_MOST = PASS_LONGEST
    if lockdown_root is not None:
        LOCKDOWN = True
        LOCKDOWN_ROOT = lockdown_root
        SIGNERS = os.path.join(lockdown_root, "allowed_signers")
    else:
        LOCKDOWN_ROOT = "/Library/Application Support/Seal"


def lockdown_installed():
    return os.path.exists(os.path.join(LOCKDOWN_ROOT, "lockdown.json"))


def lockdown_problem():
    """Why the lockdown's key can't be trusted, in words. None when it can: the key file and its folder
    must be there and not writable by this user (they belong to root)."""
    if not os.path.isfile(SIGNERS or ""):
        return "the lockdown has no phone key"
    if os.access(SIGNERS, os.W_OK) or os.access(os.path.dirname(SIGNERS), os.W_OK):
        return "the lockdown's files can be changed by this user, so they prove nothing"
    return None


class Refused(Exception):
    """Something this tool will not do, with the reason in plain words."""


# Where the words go: standard error, except for the plugin's commands, whose output the chat shows.
SAY_TO = sys.stderr


def say(text=""):
    try:
        SAY_TO.flush()  # what print() left in the text layer goes first, so the order holds
        SAY_TO.buffer.write((text + "\n").encode("utf-8", "replace"))
        SAY_TO.buffer.flush()
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        pass


def folder(*parts):
    for name in PARTS:
        path = os.path.join(FOLDER, name)
        os.makedirs(path, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        os.chmod(path, 0o700)
    return os.path.join(FOLDER, *parts)


def keep(path, fields):
    """Writes a small file whole or not at all, for this user only."""
    handle, part = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=os.path.dirname(path), suffix=".part")
    with os.fdopen(handle, "w") as out:
        json.dump(fields, out)
    os.replace(part, path)


def kept(path):
    """What a small file holds, when it holds what this tool writes. None otherwise."""
    try:
        with open(path) as handle:
            found = json.load(handle)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return found if isinstance(found, dict) else None


# In lockdown the phone's key lives in a folder only an admin can change (see `harden`).
SIGNERS = None


def allowed_signers():
    return SIGNERS or folder("allowed_signers")


def until_of(found):
    """The "until" a kept file names, when it is a number. 0 otherwise: a damaged file counts as past its
    time and is let go of, instead of stopping the lock from asking (security review L2)."""
    value = found.get("until") if isinstance(found, dict) else None
    return value if type(value) in (int, float) else 0


def purposes():
    """What the kept phone key may sign for, as its line says. None when there is no phone key."""
    try:
        with open(allowed_signers()) as handle:
            words = handle.read().split()
    except OSError:
        return None
    for word in words:
        if word.startswith('namespaces="') and word.endswith('"'):
            return word[len('namespaces="'):-1].split(",")
    return []


def key_of(command, where):
    """One name for "this exact command in this exact folder"."""
    return hashlib.sha256((command + "\0" + where).encode()).hexdigest()[:32]


def stamp(seconds):
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %z", time.localtime(seconds))


def clock(seconds):
    return time.strftime("%H:%M:%S", time.localtime(seconds))


def span(seconds):
    """A length of time in words: 30 minutes, 4 hours, 2 seconds."""
    for size, one, many in ((3600, "hour", "hours"), (60, "minute", "minutes"), (1, "second", "seconds")):
        if seconds % size == 0:
            return f"{seconds // size} {one if seconds == size else many}"


def left(until):
    seconds = max(0, int(until - time.time()))
    return span(seconds - seconds % 60 if seconds >= 60 else seconds) if seconds else "no time"


def request_text(command, where, why, asked, until, number):
    """What the phone shows and the key signs. The command is written the way JSON writes text: a line
    break, a tab or an odd letter in it shows as \\n, \\t, \\u..., so nothing can hide in it."""
    return "\n".join([
        "Seal agent gate, version 1",
        "Allow once: " + json.dumps(command, ensure_ascii=True),
        "In: " + json.dumps(where, ensure_ascii=True),
        "Held because: " + json.dumps(why, ensure_ascii=True),
        "On: " + json.dumps(socket.gethostname(), ensure_ascii=True),
        "Asked: " + stamp(asked),
        "Good until: " + stamp(until),
        "Number: " + number,
        "",
    ])


def request_line(message, namespace=NAMESPACE):
    packed = base64.urlsafe_b64encode(message).decode().rstrip("=")
    return f"seal://sign?v=1&ns={namespace}&m={packed}"


def text_of(waiting, command, where):
    """The request's words, built again from the command and the folder that are being asked about now.
    What is kept on disk only supplies the times and the number. So a kept request that was tampered
    with cannot make a yes for one command count for another: the signed words name the command."""
    try:
        return request_text(command, where, str(waiting["why"]), int(waiting["asked"]), int(waiting["until"]), str(waiting["number"]))
    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):
        return ""


def pending_path(command, where):
    return folder("pending", key_of(command, where) + ".json")


def short_lived(found):
    """A kept request's times, when they are whole numbers, it was asked no later than now, and it is good
    for five minutes at most. The kept files belong to the same user the agents run as: a request with a
    far-off end would let one signature count for years (Fable review, finding 7)."""
    asked, until = (found.get("asked"), found.get("until")) if isinstance(found, dict) else (None, None)
    if type(asked) is not int or type(until) is not int:
        return False
    return asked <= time.time() + 60 and 0 < until - asked <= 300


def read_pending(command, where):
    """The request waiting for this command, when there is one and it is still good."""
    path = pending_path(command, where)
    try:
        with open(path) as handle:
            waiting = json.load(handle)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    if (not isinstance(waiting, dict) or waiting.get("command") != command or waiting.get("in") != where
            or time.time() >= until_of(waiting) or not short_lived(waiting)):
        try:
            os.unlink(path)
        except OSError:
            pass
        return None
    return waiting


def sweep():
    """Lets go of what is past its time: old requests, and the numbers of used yeses and ended passes."""
    now = time.time()
    for part in ("pending", "used", os.path.join("pass", "ended")):
        for name in os.listdir(folder(part)):
            path = folder(part, name)
            until = until_of(kept(path))
            if now >= until + 3600:
                try:
                    os.unlink(path)
                except OSError:
                    pass


def to_clipboard(line):
    try:
        subprocess.run([COPY], input=line.encode(), check=True, timeout=20)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return False
    return True


def ask(command, where, why, copy=True, quiet=False):
    if not command.strip():
        say("seal-gate: no command to ask about.")
        return 1
    if len(command) > LONGEST_COMMAND:
        say(f"seal-gate: that command is longer than a phone can show to be read ({LONGEST_COMMAND} characters). Not asked.")
        return 1
    if not os.path.exists(allowed_signers()):
        say("seal-gate: no phone key yet. Run: seal-gate --setup \"<the line from Seal's Sign page, Copy SSH key>\"")
        return 1
    sweep()
    waiting = read_pending(command, where)
    if waiting is None:
        asked = int(time.time())
        until = asked + GOOD_FOR
        number = secrets.token_hex(16)
        waiting = {"command": command, "in": where, "why": why, "asked": asked, "until": until, "number": number}
        keep(pending_path(command, where), waiting)
    line = request_line(text_of(waiting, command, where).encode())
    if copy and not to_clipboard(line):
        say("seal-gate: the request could not be put on the clipboard. Copy the line below by hand.")
    if not quiet:
        say()
        say("Seal: a yes is wanted from your phone for this command.")
        say()
        say("    " + command)
        say("    in " + where)
        say()
        say("1. In the Seal app: Sign, Paste a signing request" + (" (it is on the clipboard)." if copy else "."))
        say("2. Read it there, Sign with Face ID, Copy the signature.")
        say(f"3. It is good until {stamp(waiting['until'])}.")
        say()
    print(line)
    return 0


def split_signature(text):
    """Picks one whole signature out of text, however its lines were broken on the way (a chat may
    turn them into spaces). Gives the signature the way ssh-keygen reads it, and the words around it.
    The signature is None when there is none."""
    end = text.find(END)
    start = text.rfind(BEGIN, 0, end) if end >= 0 else -1
    if start < 0:
        return None, text
    packed = "".join(text[start + len(BEGIN):end].split())
    letters = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/="
    if not packed or len(packed) > LONGEST_SIGNATURE or not all(letter in letters for letter in packed):
        return None, text
    lines = [packed[index:index + 70] for index in range(0, len(packed), 70)]
    return "\n".join([BEGIN] + lines + [END]) + "\n", text[:start] + text[end + len(END):]


def signature_in(text):
    return split_signature(text)[0]


def from_clipboard(wait=20):
    try:
        return subprocess.run([PASTE], capture_output=True, timeout=wait).stdout.decode(errors="replace")
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return ""


def mark_of(signature):
    return hashlib.sha256("".join(signature.split()).encode()).hexdigest()[:32]


def remember_taken(signature):
    """Notes that this Mac has used that signature. A hold may write a new request over a used one on
    the clipboard; one not noted here may be on its way from the phone, and is left alone."""
    path = folder("taken.json")
    marks = (kept(path) or {}).get("marks")
    marks = [mark for mark in marks if isinstance(mark, str)][-15:] if isinstance(marks, list) else []
    keep(path, {"marks": marks + [mark_of(signature)]})


def was_taken(signature):
    marks = (kept(folder("taken.json")) or {}).get("marks")
    return isinstance(marks, list) and mark_of(signature) in marks


def signed_by_the_phone(message, signature, namespace):
    """The real ssh-keygen is the judge: the phone's key, this purpose, exactly these bytes."""
    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile("w", suffix=".sig", delete=False) as handle:
        handle.write(signature)
        sig_path = handle.name
    try:
        verdict = subprocess.run(
            [SSH_KEYGEN, "-Y", "verify", "-f", allowed_signers(), "-I", WHO, "-n", namespace, "-s", sig_path],
            input=message.encode(), capture_output=True, timeout=10,
        )
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return False
    finally:
        os.unlink(sig_path)
    return verdict.returncode == 0


def check(command, where, text=None, quiet=False):
    """0 when a signed yes for exactly this command is there and good. A yes is used up by this."""
    def no(why):
        if not quiet:
            say("seal-gate: " + why)
        return 1

    waiting = read_pending(command, where)
    if waiting is None:
        return no("nothing is waiting for a yes for this command here (never asked, used already, or past its time).")
    number = str(waiting.get("number", ""))
    message = text_of(waiting, command, where)
    if not message or len(number) != 32 or not all(letter in "0123456789abcdef" for letter in number):
        return no("the request kept for this command is damaged. Ask again.")
    used = folder("used", number + ".json")
    if os.path.exists(used):
        return no("that yes was used already. A yes counts once.")
    signature = signature_in(text if text is not None else from_clipboard())
    if signature is None:
        return no("no signature found. Copy it in the Seal app after signing, then try again.")
    if not signed_by_the_phone(message, signature, NAMESPACE):
        return no("the signature on the clipboard is not a yes from your phone for this request. Nothing was allowed.")

    # Used up before anything is allowed, and only one asker can use it up: the file is made new or not at all.
    try:
        marker = os.open(used, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600)
    except FileExistsError:
        return no("that yes was used already. A yes counts once.")
    with os.fdopen(marker, "w") as handle:
        json.dump({"until": waiting["until"], "command": command, "in": where, "at": int(time.time())}, handle)
    remember_taken(signature)
    try:
        os.unlink(pending_path(command, where))
    except OSError:
        pass
    if not quiet:
        say("seal-gate: yes, signed by your phone. Allowed once: " + command)
    return 0


# ---------- the pass: agent sessions run nothing while none is good ----------

class turn:
    """One caller at a time for whatever makes, takes or ends a pass. Many sessions hit the lock at once."""

    def __enter__(self):
        self.handle = open(folder("pass", "turn"), "w")
        fcntl.flock(self.handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *wrong):
        self.handle.close()
        return False


def pass_text(asked, until, number):
    """What the phone shows and the key signs for a pass."""
    return "\n".join([
        "Seal session pass, version 1",
        "Unlocks: agent sessions, every tool",
        "On: " + json.dumps(socket.gethostname(), ensure_ascii=True),
        "For: " + span(until - asked),
        "Asked: " + stamp(asked),
        "Good until: " + stamp(until),
        "Number: " + number,
        "",
    ])


def pass_fields(found):
    """The times and the number out of a kept request or pass, when they are what this tool writes.
    These files belong to the same user the agents run as, so nothing in them is taken on trust."""
    try:
        asked, until, number = found["asked"], found["until"], found["number"]
    except (KeyError, TypeError):
        return None
    if type(asked) is not int or type(until) is not int or not isinstance(number, str):
        return None
    if len(number) != 32 or not all(letter in "0123456789abcdef" for letter in number):
        return None
    if not 0 < until - asked <= PASS_LONGEST:
        return None
    return asked, until, number


def pass_ended(number):
    return os.path.exists(folder("pass", "ended", number + ".json"))


def no_pass_possible():
    """Why the kept phone key cannot sign a pass, in words. None when it can."""
    allowed = purposes()
    if allowed is None:
        return "no phone key yet. Run: seal-gate --setup \"<the line from Seal's Sign page, Copy SSH key>\""
    if PASS_NAMESPACE not in allowed:
        return ("the phone key kept here may say yes to single commands only (it was set up before there were passes). "
                "Run seal-gate --setup again with the same line.")
    return None


def pass_waiting():
    """The request for a pass that waits for the phone's answer, when one does."""
    fields = pass_fields(kept(folder("pass", "asked.json")))
    if fields is None:
        return None
    asked, until, number = fields
    if not asked <= time.time() < min(until, asked + GOOD_FOR) or pass_ended(number):
        return None
    return fields


def pass_held():
    """The pass in force, as (its end, None). Or (None, why there is none)."""
    found = kept(folder("pass", "held.json"))
    if found is None:
        return None, "there is none"
    fields, signature = pass_fields(found), found.get("signature")
    if fields is None or not isinstance(signature, str):
        return None, "the kept one is damaged"
    asked, until, number = fields
    now = time.time()
    if now >= until:
        return None, f"it ran out at {clock(until)}"
    if now < asked:
        return None, "the kept one is for a time that is not here yet"
    if pass_ended(number):
        return None, "it was ended by hand"
    # Every time, not once: the kept file is only words until the phone's key says they are its own.
    if not signed_by_the_phone(pass_text(asked, until, number), signature, PASS_NAMESPACE):
        return None, "the kept one is not signed by your phone"
    return until, None


def pass_take(text):
    """Looks in text for the phone's answer to the waiting request. A good one is the pass from now on:
    (its end, None). Otherwise (None, why not)."""
    signature = signature_in(text)
    if signature is None:
        return None, "no signature found"
    with turn():
        fields = pass_waiting()
        if fields is None:
            return None, "no request for a pass waits for an answer (never asked, or asked more than five minutes ago)"
        asked, until, number = fields
        if not signed_by_the_phone(pass_text(asked, until, number), signature, PASS_NAMESPACE):
            return None, "that signature is not a pass from your phone for the request that waits"
        keep(folder("pass", "held.json"), {"asked": asked, "until": until, "number": number, "signature": signature})
        remember_taken(signature)
        try:
            os.unlink(folder("pass", "asked.json"))
        except OSError:
            pass
        return until, None


def pass_request(length=None):
    """The request for a pass that waits for the phone, made now when none waits: (its line, the pass's
    end, when the answer has to be here, whether it was made just now). Told a length, it asks for that
    length; told none, it takes what waits, or the usual."""
    why = no_pass_possible()
    if why is not None:
        raise Refused(why)
    with turn():
        sweep()
        fields = pass_waiting()
        wanted = min(length or PASS_USUAL, PASS_AT_MOST)
        made = fields is None or (length is not None and fields[1] - fields[0] != wanted)
        if made:
            asked = int(time.time())
            fields = (asked, asked + wanted, secrets.token_hex(16))
            keep(folder("pass", "asked.json"), {"asked": fields[0], "until": fields[1], "number": fields[2]})
        return request_line(pass_text(*fields).encode(), PASS_NAMESPACE), fields[1], min(fields[1], fields[0] + GOOD_FOR), made


def pass_ask(length, copy=True, quiet=False):
    if length > PASS_LONGEST:
        say(f"seal-gate: a pass is {span(PASS_LONGEST)} at most. Asking for that.")
    try:
        line, until, answer_by, _ = pass_request(length)
    except Refused as no:
        say(f"seal-gate: {no}")
        return 1
    if copy and not to_clipboard(line):
        say("seal-gate: the request could not be put on the clipboard. Copy the line below by hand.")
    if not quiet:
        held, _ = pass_held()
        say()
        say("Seal: a pass is wanted from your phone. While it is good, agent sessions on this Mac run their tools.")
        say()
        say(f"    good until {clock(until)}")
        if held is not None:
            say(f"    (a pass is good now, until {clock(held)}; the new one takes its place once signed)")
        say()
        say("1. On your phone: Seal, Sign, Paste a signing request" + (" (it is on this Mac's clipboard)." if copy else "."))
        say("2. Read it there, Sign with Face ID, Copy the signature.")
        say("3. Paste it into a message here and send." if SAY_TO is sys.stdout else
            "3. Paste it into a message to Claude and send, or run seal-gate pass check (it looks on the clipboard).")
        say(f"4. The request waits for its answer until {clock(answer_by)}.")
        say()
    print(line)
    return 0


def pass_check(text=None, quiet=False):
    """0 while a pass is good. A signed answer to a waiting request is taken first."""
    took_why = None
    if text is not None or pass_waiting() is not None:
        _, took_why = pass_take(text if text is not None else from_clipboard())
    until, why = pass_held()
    if until is None:
        if not quiet:
            say(f"seal-gate: no pass is good: {why}. Agent sessions under the lock run nothing.")
            if took_why is not None and text is not None:
                say(f"seal-gate: {took_why}.")
        return 1
    if not quiet:
        say(f"seal-gate: a pass signed by your phone is good until {clock(until)} ({left(until)} left).")
    return 0


def pass_drop():
    """Locks again now. A good pass is ended, and so is a request asked while it was good (for a longer
    one, say); their numbers are kept as ended, so the same signatures cannot be put back. With no pass
    good it was locked already, and a request that waits for the phone stays: it is the person's way
    back in. (Ending it in Seth's first real test, 2026-11-15, made the next hold write a new request
    over the clipboard the signature was coming to.)"""
    with turn():
        ended, _ = pass_held()
        for name in ("held.json", "asked.json") if ended is not None else ("held.json",):
            fields = pass_fields(kept(folder("pass", name)))
            if fields is not None:
                keep(folder("pass", "ended", fields[2] + ".json"), {"until": fields[1], "at": int(time.time())})
            try:
                os.unlink(folder("pass", name))
            except OSError:
                pass
        waiting = pass_waiting()
    if ended is not None:
        say(f"seal-gate: locked. The pass that was good until {clock(ended)} is ended.")
    else:
        say("seal-gate: locked already: no pass was good.")
        if waiting is not None:
            say(f"seal-gate: the request for a pass still waits for your phone, until {clock(min(waiting[1], waiting[0] + GOOD_FOR))}.")
    return 0


def pass_by_hand(length):
    """One round by hand: asks for a pass and waits for the phone's answer, to see how the trip feels."""
    if pass_ask(length) != 0:
        return 1
    say("Waiting up to 3 minutes for the signature to arrive on this Mac's clipboard…")
    started = time.time()
    while time.time() - started < 180:
        arrived = from_clipboard()
        if signature_in(arrived) is not None:
            until, why = pass_take(arrived)
            if until is None:
                say(f"seal-gate: a signature arrived, but {why}.")
                return 1
            say(f"seal-gate: a pass signed by your phone, {time.time() - started:.0f} seconds after asking. It is good until {clock(until)}.")
            say("seal-gate: nothing is under the lock unless a session was started with its settings. To end the pass now: seal-gate pass drop")
            return 0
        time.sleep(1.0)
    say("seal-gate: no signature arrived. The request is still on the clipboard if you want to look at where it got stuck.")
    return 1


HOW = "On your phone: Seal, Sign, Paste a signing request, Sign with Face ID, Copy the signature."


def home_short(path):
    home = own_home()
    return "~" + path[len(home):] if path.startswith(home + os.sep) else path


def way_out():
    """The way out for a person at this Mac who can't get a pass: said where they read it, so nobody is
    stuck inside Claude again (Seth's first real test, 2026-11-15). Anyone at the keyboard can open the
    Terminal app anyway; lockdown keeps its door behind the Mac's password."""
    if LOCKDOWN or lockdown_installed():
        return f'Stuck? Lockdown comes off with your Mac\'s password: in the Terminal app, sudo sh "{lockdown_tool()}" remove'
    return f"Stuck? In the Terminal app: rm {home_short(switch())}"


def held_message(line, until, answer_by, made, copied, sent_the_request=False):
    """What a person reads when the lock holds their message. The desktop app shows it as text under
    "A hook blocked your prompt" while it is the latest thing in the chat, so the first two lines are
    the whole story: what to do, and the way out."""
    if made and copied:
        where = "The request is on this Mac's clipboard for your phone, and it is the line at the bottom."
    elif made:
        where = ("The clipboard holds a signature this Mac has not used, so the request was left off it: "
                 "copy the line at the bottom to your phone.")
    else:
        where = "The request went on this Mac's clipboard when it was made, and it is the line at the bottom."
    lines = [f"Locked. {HOW} Then paste it here and send.", way_out()]
    if sent_the_request:
        lines.append("That message held the request, not the signature: the phone's copy did not reach this Mac. "
                     "Handoff has to be on, on both (iPhone: Settings, General, AirPlay & Continuity; "
                     "Mac: System Settings, General, AirDrop & Handoff). Or paste the signature from the phone "
                     "through Remote Control.")
    lines += [f"{where} It waits for your phone until {clock(answer_by)}; the pass would last until {clock(until)}.", "", line]
    return "\n".join(lines)


def held_tool(line):
    """What the agent is told when the lock holds a tool."""
    return "\n".join([
        "Seal lock: agent sessions on this Mac are locked, so this tool did not run. Nothing runs until the person's phone signs a pass.",
        "This is the person's step, not yours. Tell them the session is locked and show them the request line below, whole.",
        f"{HOW} Then they paste the signature into a message here and send it.",
        "Do not try another tool, and do not look for a way around this. Stop and wait for them.",
        "",
        line,
    ])


def lock(event):
    """The lock's verdict on one hook event: ("go", words for the agent or "") or ("hold", words)."""
    kind = event.get("hook_event_name")
    said = event.get("prompt") if kind == "UserPromptSubmit" else None
    said = said if isinstance(said, str) else None

    # The plugin's own commands that cannot open anything go through, typed alone: the person can see
    # where the lock stands, end a pass, and read how lockdown works.
    if said is not None and LET_THROUGH.fullmatch(said.strip()):
        return "go", ""

    # The phone's answer inside the message: the usual way, since a paste on the Mac fetches the
    # signature from the phone at that moment, and the only way far from the Mac.
    arrived = said is not None and BEGIN in said and pass_take(said)[0] is not None
    if said is not None and BEGIN in said and not arrived and off_by_message(said):
        return "go", ("Seal: the signature in this message is the person's yes, signed on their phone, to turning the Seal lock off. "
                      "The lock is off now: sessions on this Mac run as usual. Say so in one line.")
    until, _ = pass_held()
    clip = None
    if until is None:
        # Read once: a signature the phone left on the shared clipboard is taken, and one that may still
        # be on its way is never written over.
        clip = from_clipboard(CLIPBOARD_WAIT)
        if pass_waiting() is not None:
            until, _ = pass_take(clip)
    if until is not None:
        if arrived:
            # The message goes on to the agent with a word about what the signature was. (Holding a message
            # that is nothing but the signature would read as "blocked" just when the lock opens.)
            rest = (" Tell the person in one line that it is unlocked, then do what the rest of the message asks."
                    if split_signature(said)[1].strip() else
                    " The message holds nothing else: say so in one line and wait for what they want.")
            return "go", f"Seal: the signature in this message is a pass signed on the person's phone. Agent sessions on this Mac are unlocked until {clock(until)}.{rest}"
        return "go", ""

    try:
        line, until, answer_by, made = pass_request()
    except Refused as no:
        return "hold", f"Locked, and nothing can unlock it yet: {no}\n{way_out()}"
    fresh = signature_in(clip or "")
    copied = made and (fresh is None or was_taken(fresh)) and to_clipboard(line)
    if said is None:
        return "hold", held_tool(line)
    sent_the_request = "seal://sign?" in said and BEGIN not in said
    return "hold", held_message(line, until, answer_by, made, copied, sent_the_request)


def hold(kind, words):
    """Holds what the hook was asked about. A message is held with Claude Code's JSON answer and exit 0:
    the desktop app shows its reason as text, while with exit 2 it puts the hook's own command line in
    front of the words. A tool, or anything that isn't a message, is held with exit 2, whose words go
    to the agent. If the JSON can't be written, exit 2 holds the message too."""
    if kind == "UserPromptSubmit":
        try:
            sys.stdout.write(json.dumps({"decision": "block", "reason": words}))
            sys.stdout.flush()
            return 0
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            pass
    say(words)
    return 2


def hook(options=()):
    """What an agent's hooks call before a message is taken and before a tool runs. Lets it go on to the
    agent's own rules (exit 0, saying nothing or a word for the agent), or holds it (see `hold`).
    Whatever goes wrong in here holds.

    --hardened                      the plugin's hook: nothing taken from the surroundings
    --lockdown [--root DIR] [--state DIR] [--copy CMD --paste CMD]
                                    the admin-owned hook: always on; the paths come only from these
                                    arguments, which live in a root-owned file"""
    kind = None
    try:
        options = list(options)
        try:
            event = json.loads(sys.stdin.buffer.read().decode("utf-8", "replace"))
        except ValueError:
            event = {}
        event = event if isinstance(event, dict) else {}
        # Only a well-formed message is answered with JSON; anything else is held with exit 2.
        kind = "UserPromptSubmit" if event.get("hook_event_name") == "UserPromptSubmit" and isinstance(event.get("prompt"), str) else None
        if "--lockdown" in options:
            def given(flag):
                return options[options.index(flag) + 1] if flag in options[:-1] else None
            harden(lockdown_root=given("--root") or LOCKDOWN_ROOT, state=given("--state"),
                   copy=given("--copy"), paste=given("--paste"))
            problem = lockdown_problem()
            if problem is not None:
                return hold(kind, f"Locked down, and {problem}. Nothing runs. "
                                  f'In the Terminal app: sudo sh "{lockdown_tool()}" status')
        elif "--hardened" in options:
            harden()
        # Nothing but the verdict reaches standard output: on a held message, Claude Code reads it as the
        # JSON answer, and stray words there would read as context and let the message through.
        with contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):
            verdict, words = lock(event)
        if verdict == "go":
            if words:
                sys.stdout.write(words)
                sys.stdout.flush()
            return 0
        return hold(kind, words)
    except BaseException as wrong:
        say(f"Seal lock: something went wrong inside the lock ({type(wrong).__name__}), so nothing runs. "
            "Stuck? In the Terminal app: rm ~/.seal-gate/lock-on")
        return 2


def settings():
    """The settings that put a Claude Code session under the lock. Messages and tools both go through
    it, and `onFailure` makes a lock that cannot start, breaks or takes too long hold as well: without
    it, Claude Code lets the message or the tool go ahead."""
    one = {"type": "command", "command": "/usr/bin/env",
           "args": ["-i", "LANG=en_US.UTF-8", "/usr/bin/python3", "-I", os.path.realpath(__file__), "hook", "--hardened"],
           "onFailure": "block"}
    print(json.dumps({"hooks": {
        "UserPromptSubmit": [{"hooks": [one]}],
        "PreToolUse": [{"matcher": "*", "hooks": [one]}],
    }}, indent=2))
    return 0


def passes(arguments):
    verb, options = arguments[0], arguments[1:]
    known = {"ask": ("--no-copy", "--quiet"), "check": ("--stdin", "--quiet"), "drop": (), "status": (), "try": ()}
    if verb not in known:
        say("seal-gate: see seal-gate --help.")
        return 2
    flags, length, index = set(), PASS_USUAL, 0
    while index < len(options):
        if verb in ("ask", "try") and options[index] == "--for" and index + 1 < len(options):
            try:
                minutes = int(options[index + 1])
            except ValueError:
                minutes = 0
            if minutes < 1:
                say("seal-gate: --for takes a number of minutes, 1 or more.")
                return 2
            length = minutes * 60
            index += 2
        elif options[index] in known[verb]:
            flags.add(options[index])
            index += 1
        else:
            say(f"seal-gate: I don't know {options[index]}.")
            return 2
    if verb == "ask":
        return pass_ask(length, copy="--no-copy" not in flags, quiet="--quiet" in flags)
    if verb == "check":
        return pass_check(text=sys.stdin.read() if "--stdin" in flags else None, quiet="--quiet" in flags)
    if verb == "drop":
        return pass_drop()
    if verb == "try":
        return pass_by_hand(length)
    return status()


def setup(key_line):
    # Whoever could pair a key of their own could sign their own passes: never while the lock is on, by
    # this road or /seal:pair (security review M2).
    if lock_is_on():
        say("seal-gate: the lock is on, so no new phone key is taken. Turn the lock off first (with your phone), then pair.")
        return 1
    key_line = " ".join(key_line.split())
    if "PRIVATE" in key_line:
        say("seal-gate: that is a private key. It was not kept. The public key line starts with ecdsa-sha2-nistp256 or ssh-ed25519.")
        return 1
    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile("w", suffix=".pub", delete=False) as handle:
        handle.write(key_line + "\n")
        key_path = handle.name
    try:
        listed = subprocess.run([SSH_KEYGEN, "-l", "-f", key_path], capture_output=True, text=True)
    finally:
        os.unlink(key_path)
    parts = listed.stdout.split()
    if listed.returncode != 0 or len(parts) < 2:
        say("seal-gate: that is not an SSH public key line. Copy it from the Seal app's Sign page (Copy SSH key).")
        return 1
    path = allowed_signers()
    with open(path + ".part", "w") as handle:
        handle.write(f'{WHO} namespaces="{NAMESPACE},{PASS_NAMESPACE}" {key_line}\n')
    os.chmod(path + ".part", 0o600)
    os.replace(path + ".part", path)
    say(f"seal-gate: a yes for a command and a pass now have to come from the key {parts[1]}.")
    say(f"seal-gate: kept in {path}. Remove that file to undo.")
    return 0


def status():
    with turn():
        sweep()
    allowed = purposes()
    if allowed is None:
        say("seal-gate: no phone key yet (seal-gate --setup).")
    else:
        with open(allowed_signers()) as handle:
            say("seal-gate: the phone key: " + " ".join(handle.read().split()[2:4])[:60] + "…")
        if PASS_NAMESPACE not in allowed:
            say("seal-gate: that key may say yes to single commands only. For passes, run seal-gate --setup again with the same line.")
    until, why = pass_held()
    if until is not None:
        say(f"seal-gate: a pass is good until {clock(until)} ({left(until)} left). Agent sessions under the lock run their tools.")
    else:
        say(f"seal-gate: no pass is good: {why}. Agent sessions under the lock take no message and run no tool.")
    asked = pass_waiting()
    if asked is not None:
        say(f"seal-gate: a request for a pass waits for the phone's answer until {clock(min(asked[1], asked[0] + GOOD_FOR))}.")
    waiting = []
    for name in sorted(os.listdir(folder("pending"))):
        item = kept(folder("pending", name))
        if item is not None and time.time() < until_of(item):
            waiting.append(item)
    if not waiting:
        say("seal-gate: nothing is waiting for a yes.")
    for item in waiting:
        say(f"seal-gate: waiting until {stamp(item['until'])}: {item['command']}  (in {item['in']})")
    return 0


def by_hand():
    """One round with a harmless made-up command, to see how the trip to the phone and back feels."""
    command = "echo seal-gate hand test " + secrets.token_hex(3)
    where = os.getcwd()
    if ask(command, where, "a hand test: nothing will run") != 0:
        return 1
    say("Waiting up to 3 minutes for the signature to arrive on this Mac's clipboard…")
    started = time.time()
    while time.time() - started < 180:
        arrived = from_clipboard()
        if signature_in(arrived) is not None:
            if check(command, where, text=arrived, quiet=True) == 0:
                say(f"seal-gate: yes, signed by your phone, {time.time() - started:.0f} seconds after asking. The trip works.")
                return 0
            say("seal-gate: a signature arrived, but it is not a yes from your phone for this request.")
            return 1
        time.sleep(1.0)
    say("seal-gate: no signature arrived. The request is still on the clipboard if you want to look at where it got stuck.")
    return 1


# ---------- the switch: the plugin's /seal:on and /seal:off ----------

OFF_WORDS = "Turn the Seal lock off"
OFF_WHY = "someone typed /seal:off"
# The plugin's commands a held message may still be, typed alone. None of them opens anything, and none
# writes the clipboard or replaces a waiting request: /seal:off and /seal:pass are held like any message
# while no pass is good, so a sender who can't sign can't swap what the person is about to sign
# (Fable review, finding 6).
LET_THROUGH = re.compile(r"/seal:(status|on|drop|lockdown)")
KEY_KINDS = ("ecdsa-sha2-nistp256 ", "ssh-ed25519 ")


def switch():
    """The file that says the lock is on. The plugin's seal-hook looks for it before starting Python."""
    return folder("lock-on")


def lock_is_on():
    return LOCKDOWN or lockdown_installed() or os.path.lexists(switch())


def switch_off():
    try:
        os.unlink(switch())
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass


def off_where():
    return os.path.realpath(FOLDER)


def phone_key_line():
    """The phone's public key line as it was paired, or None."""
    try:
        with open(allowed_signers()) as handle:
            words = handle.read().split()
    except OSError:
        return None
    return " ".join(words[2:]) if len(words) >= 4 else None


def off_by_message(said):
    """A yes from the phone to turning the lock off, pasted into a message. True when it switched it off.
    Never in lockdown: that takes the Mac's admin password."""
    if LOCKDOWN or lockdown_installed():
        return False
    if not lock_is_on() or read_pending(OFF_WORDS, off_where()) is None:
        return False
    if check(OFF_WORDS, off_where(), text=said, quiet=True) != 0:
        return False
    switch_off()
    return True


def lockdown_tool():
    """The lockdown script to name to the person. Once lockdown is in, its own root-owned copy: running
    the plugin's copy with sudo would let whoever can edit the plugin folder run code as root (Fable
    review, finding 2)."""
    installed = os.path.join(LOCKDOWN_ROOT, "seal-lockdown")
    if lockdown_installed() and os.path.exists(installed):
        return installed
    return os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "seal-lockdown")


def turn_on():
    if lockdown_installed():
        say("Seal: lockdown is on, so the lock is always on. /seal:status shows where it stands.")
        return 0
    why = no_pass_possible()
    if why is not None:
        say(f"Seal: the lock was not turned on: {why}")
        say("Pair your phone first: in the Seal app, Sign page, Copy SSH key. Then /seal:pair.")
        return 1
    if lock_is_on():
        say("Seal: the lock is already on.")
    else:
        keep(switch(), {"since": int(time.time())})
        say("Seal: the lock is on. Every Claude Code session on this Mac that has the Seal plugin, this one too, now waits "
            "for a pass signed on your phone before it takes a message or runs a tool.")
    until, _ = pass_held()
    if until is not None:
        say(f"A pass is good until {clock(until)}, so sessions run until then. To lock now: /seal:drop")
    else:
        say(f"Your next message asks your phone for a pass ({span(PASS_USUAL)}; for longer, /seal:pass 120).")
    say("Turning it off needs your phone too: /seal:off")
    say(way_out())
    return 0


def turn_off(text=None):
    """The lock goes off only on a yes signed by the phone for exactly that, taken from the clipboard (or
    from text). Without one it asks, and the request waits five minutes for the answer."""
    if lockdown_installed():
        say("Seal: lockdown is on. Turning it off takes your Mac's password, so no agent can. In Terminal:")
        say()
        say(f'sudo sh "{lockdown_tool()}" remove')
        return 0
    if not lock_is_on():
        say("Seal: the lock is already off. /seal:on turns it on.")
        return 0
    where = off_where()
    if read_pending(OFF_WORDS, where) is not None:
        arrived = text if text is not None else from_clipboard()
        if signature_in(arrived) is not None:
            if check(OFF_WORDS, where, text=arrived, quiet=True) == 0:
                switch_off()
                say("Seal: the lock is off. Your phone said yes. Sessions on this Mac run as usual.")
                return 0
            say("Seal: the signature on the clipboard is not your phone's yes to turning the lock off. The lock stays on.")
            say()
    say("Seal: turning the lock off needs a yes from your phone.")
    say("1. On your phone: Seal, Sign, Paste a signing request (it is on this Mac's clipboard).")
    say(f"2. It reads \"{OFF_WORDS}\". Sign with Face ID, Copy the signature.")
    say("3. Paste it into a message here and send.")
    say(way_out())
    say()
    status_code = ask(OFF_WORDS, where, OFF_WHY, quiet=True)
    waiting = read_pending(OFF_WORDS, where)
    if status_code == 0 and waiting is not None:
        say(f"The request waits for its answer until {clock(waiting['until'])}.")
    return status_code


def pair(text=None):
    """Keeps the phone's public key, from the clipboard unless given. Never while the lock is on: whoever
    could pair a key of their own could sign their own passes."""
    if lockdown_installed():
        say("Seal: lockdown is on, so a new phone key goes in with your Mac's password. Copy the key on the phone, then in Terminal:")
        say()
        say(f'sudo sh "{lockdown_tool()}" pair "$(pbpaste)"')
        return 1
    if lock_is_on():
        say("Seal: the lock is on, so no new phone key is taken. Turn the lock off first (/seal:off, with your phone), then pair.")
        return 1
    found = text if text is not None else from_clipboard()
    if "PRIVATE KEY" in found:
        say("Seal: that is a private key. It was not kept, and it should not be on a clipboard. "
            "The line to pair is the public one, from the Seal app's Sign page: Copy SSH key.")
        return 1
    line = next((each.strip() for each in found.splitlines() if each.strip().startswith(KEY_KINDS)), None)
    if line is None:
        say("Seal: no phone key on the clipboard. In the Seal app: Sign page, Copy SSH key. Then /seal:pair again.")
        return 1
    before = phone_key_line()
    if setup(line) != 0:
        return 1
    if before is not None and before.split()[:2] != line.split()[:2]:
        say("Seal: the key paired before was replaced. Passes and yeses from it no longer count.")
    say("Next: /seal:on locks Claude Code sessions on this Mac. /seal:git signs commits in a repository.")
    return 0


def git_here():
    """Sets up the repository in the current folder to sign commits through the phone. seal-git-sign is
    copied to this tool's folder first, so git keeps finding it after the plugin updates."""
    line = phone_key_line()
    if line is None:
        say("Seal: no phone key yet. In the Seal app: Sign page, Copy SSH key. Then /seal:pair.")
        return 1
    source = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "seal-git-sign")
    target = folder("bin", "seal-git-sign")
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(target), mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    shutil.copyfile(source, target + ".part")
    os.chmod(target + ".part", 0o700)
    os.replace(target + ".part", target)
    done = subprocess.run([sys.executable, target, "--setup", line], capture_output=True, text=True)
    for each in (done.stdout + done.stderr).splitlines():
        say(each.replace("seal-git-sign: ", "Seal: ", 1))
    if done.returncode != 0:
        return 1
    say("To sign every commit here: git config commit.gpgsign true")
    say("When git asks, the request goes on the clipboard and a notice shows: Seal, Sign, Paste a signing request, "
        "Sign with Face ID, Copy the signature. git waits up to two minutes for it.")
    return 0


def fingerprint(key_line):
    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile("w", suffix=".pub", delete=False) as handle:
        handle.write(key_line + "\n")
        key_path = handle.name
    try:
        listed = subprocess.run([SSH_KEYGEN, "-l", "-f", key_path], capture_output=True, text=True)
    finally:
        os.unlink(key_path)
    parts = listed.stdout.split()
    return parts[1] if listed.returncode == 0 and len(parts) > 1 else "(unreadable)"


def lock_status():
    """Where everything stands, in the chat's words."""
    with turn():
        sweep()
    if lockdown_installed():
        say("Seal: LOCKDOWN is on. Every Claude Code session on this Mac waits for a pass from your phone, and no "
            "project setting can switch that off. Removing it takes your Mac's password.")
        harden(lockdown_root=LOCKDOWN_ROOT)
        problem = lockdown_problem()
        if problem is not None:
            say(f"Problem: {problem}.")
        if not managed_hook_present(MANAGED_SETTINGS, os.path.join(LOCKDOWN_ROOT, "seal-gate")):
            say(f"Problem: the lockdown's hook is not in {MANAGED_SETTINGS}. The plugin still holds sessions; "
                f'to put it back: sudo sh "{lockdown_tool()}" install')
    elif lock_is_on():
        say("Seal: the lock is ON. Claude Code sessions with the Seal plugin wait for a pass from your phone.")
        say("A project's settings could still switch this off. /seal:lockdown makes it hold against that.")
    else:
        say("Seal: the lock is off. /seal:on turns it on.")
    line, allowed = phone_key_line(), purposes()
    if line is None:
        say("Phone key: none yet. In the Seal app: Sign page, Copy SSH key. Then /seal:pair.")
    else:
        say(f"Phone key: {fingerprint(line)} ({line.split()[0]}).")
        if allowed is not None and PASS_NAMESPACE not in allowed:
            say("That key may say yes to single commands only. /seal:pair again (with /seal:off first if the lock is on).")
    until, why = pass_held()
    say(f"Pass: good until {clock(until)} ({left(until)} left). /seal:drop ends it." if until is not None else f"Pass: none ({why}).")
    asked = pass_waiting()
    if asked is not None:
        say(f"Waiting for your phone: a pass, until {clock(min(asked[1], asked[0] + GOOD_FOR))}.")
    for name in sorted(os.listdir(folder("pending"))):
        item = kept(folder("pending", name))
        if item is not None and time.time() < until_of(item):
            say(f"Waiting for your phone: a yes to \"{item.get('command')}\", until {clock(item['until'])}.")
    return 0


def lockdown_help():
    if lockdown_installed():
        say("Seal: lockdown is already on. To remove it (your Mac's password), in Terminal:")
        say()
        say(f'sudo sh "{lockdown_tool()}" remove')
        return 0
    if no_pass_possible() is not None:
        say("Seal: pair your phone first (/seal:pair). Lockdown takes the key that is paired.")
        return 1
    say("Seal: lockdown puts the lock in Claude Code's admin-owned settings. Then:")
    say("- every Claude Code session on this Mac waits for a pass from your phone, this one too;")
    say("- no project, local or user setting can switch it off (a plain /seal:on can be);")
    say("- removing it, or pairing another phone, takes your Mac's password, which no agent has;")
    say("- scheduled jobs that run Claude (a nightly check, an agent job) wait for a pass too.")
    say()
    say("To turn it on, open the Terminal app (not Claude) and paste this. It shows your phone key's fingerprint and asks before it changes anything:")
    say()
    say(f'sudo sh "{lockdown_tool()}" install')
    return 0


def lockdown_entry(gate, root, python="/usr/bin/python3"):
    """The hook the lockdown puts in Claude Code's admin-owned settings. Run with `args`, so no shell
    takes part, with an empty environment and Python in isolated mode, named by its real root-owned
    path rather than Apple's /usr/bin stand-in: nothing from the session or a project reaches it."""
    return {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "/usr/bin/env",
        "args": ["-i", "LANG=en_US.UTF-8", python, "-I", gate, "hook", "--lockdown", "--root", root],
        "timeout": 45,
        "onFailure": "block",
    }


def is_ours(entry, gate):
    return isinstance(entry, dict) and entry.get("command") == "/usr/bin/env" and gate in (entry.get("args") or [])


def managed_hook_present(path, gate):
    found = kept(path)
    hooks = (found or {}).get("hooks") if isinstance(found, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(hooks, dict):
        return False
    return all(any(is_ours(each, gate) for group in (hooks.get(event) or []) if isinstance(group, dict)
                   for each in (group.get("hooks") or []))
               for event in ("UserPromptSubmit", "PreToolUse"))


def root_owned_python():
    """This Python's real path, when it and every folder above it belong to root and only root can
    write them. None otherwise. Used by seal-lockdown, as root, to name the interpreter in the hook."""
    path = os.path.realpath(sys.executable)
    walk = path
    while True:
        info = os.lstat(walk)
        if info.st_uid != 0 or info.st_mode & 0o022:
            return None
        parent = os.path.dirname(walk)
        if parent == walk:
            return path
        walk = parent


def managed(verb, path, gate, root, python="/usr/bin/python3"):
    """Adds the lockdown's two hooks to Claude Code's managed settings file, or takes them out again,
    leaving everything else in the file as it was. Used by seal-lockdown, as root."""
    found = {}
    if os.path.exists(path):
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as handle:
            found = json.load(handle)
        if not isinstance(found, dict):
            raise Refused(f"{path} is not a settings object; nothing was changed")
    hooks = found.get("hooks") or {}
    if not isinstance(hooks, dict):
        raise Refused(f"the hooks in {path} are not an object; nothing was changed")
    for event in ("UserPromptSubmit", "PreToolUse"):
        groups = [group for group in (hooks.get(event) or [])
                  if not (isinstance(group, dict) and any(is_ours(each, gate) for each in group.get("hooks") or []))]
        if verb == "add":
            group = {"hooks": [lockdown_entry(gate, root, python)]}
            if event == "PreToolUse":
                group = {"matcher": "*", **group}
            groups.append(group)
        if groups:
            hooks[event] = groups
        else:
            hooks.pop(event, None)
    if hooks:
        found["hooks"] = hooks
    else:
        found.pop("hooks", None)
    if not found:
        if os.path.exists(path):
            os.unlink(path)
        return
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    with open(path + ".part", "w", encoding="utf-8") as handle:
        json.dump(found, handle, indent=2)
        handle.write("\n")
    os.chmod(path + ".part", 0o644)
    os.replace(path + ".part", path)


def slash(arguments):
    """The plugin's /seal: commands. Their output is what the chat shows, so it goes to standard output."""
    global SAY_TO
    SAY_TO = sys.stdout
    verb, rest = (arguments[0], arguments[1:]) if arguments else ("status", [])
    if verb == "status" and not rest:
        return lock_status()
    if verb == "on" and not rest:
        return turn_on()
    if verb == "off" and not rest:
        return turn_off()
    if verb == "drop" and not rest:
        return pass_drop()
    if verb == "pair" and not rest:
        return pair()
    if verb == "git" and not rest:
        return git_here()
    if verb == "lockdown" and not rest:
        return lockdown_help()
    if verb == "pass" and len(rest) <= 1:
        try:
            minutes = int(rest[0]) if rest else PASS_USUAL // 60
        except ValueError:
            minutes = 0
        if minutes < 1:
            say("Seal: /seal:pass takes a number of minutes, like /seal:pass 120.")
            return 2
        return pass_ask(minutes * 60)
    say("Seal: the commands are /seal:status, /seal:pair, /seal:on, /seal:off, /seal:pass [minutes], /seal:drop, /seal:git and /seal:lockdown.")
    return 2


def main(arguments):
    if not arguments or arguments[0] in ("-h", "--help"):
        say(__doc__)
        return 0
    if arguments[0] == "slash":
        return slash(arguments[1:])
    if arguments[0] == "python-path" and len(arguments) == 1:
        found = root_owned_python()
        if found is None:
            say("seal-gate: this Python, or a folder above it, can be changed by someone other than root.")
            return 1
        print(found)
        return 0
    if arguments[0] == "managed" and len(arguments) in (5, 6) and arguments[1] in ("add", "remove"):
        try:
            managed(*arguments[1:])
        except (Refused, OSError, ValueError) as no:
            say(f"seal-gate: {no}")
            return 1
        return 0
    if arguments[0] == "on" and len(arguments) == 1:
        return turn_on()
    if arguments[0] == "off" and len(arguments) == 1:
        return turn_off()
    if arguments[0] == "pair" and len(arguments) <= 2:
        return pair(arguments[1] if len(arguments) == 2 else None)
    if arguments[0] == "git" and len(arguments) == 1:
        return git_here()
    if arguments[0] == "--setup" and len(arguments) == 2:
        return setup(arguments[1])
    if arguments[0] == "status" and len(arguments) == 1:
        return status()
    if arguments[0] == "try":
        return by_hand()
    if arguments[0] == "hook":
        return hook(arguments[1:])
    if arguments[0] == "settings" and len(arguments) == 1:
        return settings()
    if arguments[0] == "pass" and len(arguments) >= 2:
        return passes(arguments[1:])
    if arguments[0] in ("ask", "check") and "--" in arguments:
        split = arguments.index("--")
        # The command as a shell would read it (security review L1). Given as one argument, it is that
        # text exactly, the way a guard hands over the command it held. Given as several words, each is
        # quoted where it needs to be, so `-- echo "a b"` and `-- echo a b` are two different commands,
        # and so two different requests.
        words = arguments[split + 1:]
        options, command = arguments[1:split], words[0] if len(words) == 1 else shlex.join(words)
        where = os.getcwd()
        why = "it was held"
        index = 0
        flags = set()
        while index < len(options):
            if options[index] == "--in" and index + 1 < len(options):
                where = options[index + 1]
                index += 2
            elif options[index] == "--why" and index + 1 < len(options):
                why = options[index + 1]
                index += 2
            elif options[index] in ("--no-copy", "--quiet", "--stdin"):
                flags.add(options[index])
                index += 1
            else:
                say(f"seal-gate: I don't know {options[index]}.")
                return 2
        where = os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(where))
        if arguments[0] == "ask":
            return ask(command, where, why, copy="--no-copy" not in flags, quiet="--quiet" in flags)
        return check(command, where, text=sys.stdin.read() if "--stdin" in flags else None, quiet="--quiet" in flags)
    say("seal-gate: see seal-gate --help.")
    return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
